cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite P-System if you use this software in your research."
title: "P-System: a registry of single-owner state with quorum certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amodio"
    given-names: "Paolo"
license: "Apache-2.0"
type: software
version: "1.0.0-rc2"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaoloAmodio001/P-System"
abstract: >-
  A registry of single-owner state without global consensus: a committee of
  3f+1 validators certifies events with quorum certificates of 2f+1
  signatures, and every node derives the same state from the same set of
  certified events. Python implementation, with a Lean 4 model of the
  protocol and machine-checked safety theorems about that model; the link
  between code and model is tested, not proved.
keywords:
  - distributed systems
  - quorum certificates
  - Byzantine fault model
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
